# apps/web — frontend

Next.js **16.2** App Router, React 19, Clerk `@clerk/nextjs` v7, TanStack Query, Axios, Zustand, Tailwind 4 via `@workspace/ui`.

## Structure

- `app/` — App Router only (no `pages/`). `(dashboard)/` for authenticated shell; `sign-in`/`sign-up` catch-alls; `print/` outside dashboard chrome.
- `components/` — shared UI by domain (`qc/`, `surveys/`, `admin/`, `layout/`, …).
- `features/` — feature modules (`configuration/`, `etl/`, `master-data/`) with colocated `components/`, `hooks/`, `lib/`.
- `hooks/use-api.ts` — React Query hooks to Nest; `lib/api/client.ts` — Axios envelope helpers.
- `stores/` — Zustand (auth profile is **not** persisted).
- `proxy.ts` — **replaces `middleware.ts`** in Next 16. Do not create `middleware.ts`.

## Next.js 16 / async dynamic APIs

Params are `Promise<…>`:

```tsx
// RSC — await
export default async function Page({ params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string }> }) {
  const { id } = await params
}

// Client — use() or useParams()
"use client"
import { use } from "react"
export default function Page({ params }: { params: Promise<{ surveyId: string }> }) {
  const { surveyId } = use(params)
}
```

- Prefer client `useSearchParams()` + `router.replace`; wrap those pages in `<Suspense>`.
- Do not call `cookies()` / `headers()` from `next/headers` unless required — this app rarely uses them.
- Before using unfamiliar Next APIs, check `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` (see root `AGENTS.md`).

## RSC vs client

- **RSC:** root/`(dashboard)` layouts, redirects, thin `page.tsx` wrappers, loading/error shells.
- **Client (`"use client"`):** interactive dashboards, forms, tables, hooks, stores, providers.
- Keep route files thin: `page.tsx` → feature hub or view component.

## Clerk auth

| Layer          | Pattern                                                                                                                |
| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Edge           | `proxy.ts` → `clerkMiddleware({ signInUrl, signUpUrl })` only (session context; **no** route protection here)          |
| Root           | `app/layout.tsx` → `<ClerkProvider signInUrl="/sign-in" signUpUrl="/sign-up" …>`                                       |
| Dashboard gate | `(dashboard)/layout.tsx` → `await auth.protect()`, `getToken()`, Nest `GET /users/me`, then `forbidden()` / `redirect` |
| Client         | `useAuth()` + `ProtectedDashboardLayout`; hydrate Nest profile into Zustand                                            |
| API token      | `providers/app-providers.tsx` → `setApiTokenGetter` from `useAuth().getToken`                                          |

- Do **not** use `currentUser()` for product authz. Use Nest profile permissions via `useAuthStore.hasPermission("resource:action")`.
- Gate React Query: `enabled: isLoaded && Boolean(isSignedIn) && canView`.

## Nest API client

- Call Nest only through `lib/api/client.ts` helpers (`apiGet`/`apiPost`/…) or `hooks/use-api.ts`.
- Envelope: `{ success, message, data, errors }` — throw when `!success`. Use `getApiErrorMessage` for toasts.
- Server-side `fetch` must unwrap the same envelope (`lib/auth/unwrap-api-profile.ts`).
- `baseURL` = `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (default `http://localhost:4000`). Root env is loaded in `next.config.ts`.

## UI & imports

- Components: `@workspace/ui/components/button` (etc.). Utils: `cn` from `@workspace/ui/lib/utils`.
- Do not invent local shadcn primitives — extend `@workspace/ui`.
- App aliases: `@/components/...`, `@/hooks/...`, `@/features/...`, `@/lib/...`.
- Shared domain helpers: `@workspace/validation` (e.g. parcel/property formatters).

## Conventions

- Permission strings match Nest (`dashboard:view`, `survey:approve`, …) and `lib/navigation.ts`.
- React Query defaults: `staleTime: 30_000`, `retry: 1`, `refetchOnWindowFocus: false`.
- File names: kebab-case components (`qc-review-detail.tsx`); toasts via Sonner + `getApiErrorMessage`.
- `next.config.ts`: `output: "standalone"`, `transpilePackages: ["@workspace/ui", "@workspace/validation"]`, `experimental.authInterrupts: true` (enables `forbidden()`).
